==Battleground==
*1 [[R.Ost]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*1 [[R.Ost]] spawns after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>.
*1 [[R.Ost]] spawns after 90 seconds<sup>2,700f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Camelle]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[R.Ost]]s spawn, delay 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>.
**4 [[R.Ost]]s spawn, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
**7 [[R.Ost]]s spawn, delay 8.67~12 seconds<sup>260f~360f</sup>.
**1 [[R.Ost]] spawns.
**Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn, delay 10~30 seconds<sup>300f~900f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This can be an extremely challenging stage due to the large number of R.Osts and the backliner, Camelle, who can prove to be a challenge to many players. Having three to four meatshields can help significantly. It is heavily recommended to have units that outrange the R.Osts and also be stacked easily such as Cyborg Cat, Drama Cats, Dragon Cat variants, and many other midrangers. Mythic backliners like Ururun Cat, [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Crimson Mina]], and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] can do very good damage to the R.Osts. Crowd-controllers can be very useful, but are not necessarily required to win. Units such as [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge Cat]] and [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] can [[Weaken]] and [[Slow]] the R.Osts respectively. Haniwa Cat and Brainwashed Wall Cat are two especially effective meatshields for this stage, as they Resist the only trait here. Brainwashed Wall has higher health, but slower recharge, and Haniwa has slow speed but {{4c}} usability.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]]: A very good meatshield here as his resistance to Traitless allow him to take many hits from the R.Ost.
*[[Suntan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Macho Suntan Cat]]: Can be used as a meatshield that can [[Dodge]] an attack, but it can be difficult to constantly deploy him due to his higher cost compared to other meatshields.
*[[Brainwashed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Wall Cat]]: Can be used as a very efficient meatshield due to his Resistance to Traitless enhancing his survivability. True Form makes him viable for {{3c}} as well as coming from a Relatively easy [[Demon Eraser (Merciless)|Awakening Stage]].
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: If timed correctly, he can deal high damage to an enemy stack, or chain an R.Ost. Alternatively, you can use Bahamut's second form instead. Crazed Bahamut can land large amounts of damage every attack, knockbacking all R.Osts he hits, potentially killing them.
*[[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Lord of Ruin Jagando Jr.]]: Being Strong Against Traitless with a 100% chance to spawn a level 1 Surge that knocks back enemies on his third hit, Jagando can greatly ease replays on higher difficulties, especially {{4c}}, as long as meatshields buy him enough time to finish his foreswing.
*[[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]]: Deals gradual damage to the R.Osts and [[Knockback|knocks them back]] occasionally, allowing your units to hit the Camelle.
*[[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg/Paris Cat]]: Can  stack damage against most threats, since she has a short recharge and decent damage. Beware of her high cost. If your cash gets low, refrain from sending Cyborgs and only send more cost efficient attackers like Drama Cats.
*[[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama/Slapstick Cats]]: Has a similar usage to Cyborg, but with more cost efficiency, so it's recommended to use both together. Slapsticks can be used on higher crown difficulties for higher damage.
*[[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic King Dragon]]: Manic King Dragon, alongside other Dragon Cats, has high range and single target damage, allowing him to work well for the start of the stage.
*[[Fencer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Kitty of Liberty]]: Although they have 95 less range than Manic King Dragon, Liberty has better dps at nearly half the cost and cooldown while still comfortably outranging R.Ost, making him a stronger alternative to Dragon variants.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]]: Only available on higher crown difficulties, but serves as an impassable wall that can buy attackers more time to land their hits. Unlike traditional meatshields, Stone is guaranteed to stop the horde of R.Osts dead in their tracks, denying the R.Osts any opportunity to advance.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]]: Usable without talents, but her [[Savage Blow]] transforms her into one of the best midrangers for this stage. Her tripled damage upon landing a Savage Blow may even be high enough to force a swarm of R.Osts to stagger. As an added bonus, her [[Long Distance]] means she's almost guaranteed to hit every R.Ost on the field.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Most [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] ubers completely annihilate this stage since they are tailored specifically to Traitless enemies.
*Ubers with high nuke damage such as [[Lasvoss (Uber Rare Cat)|Lasvoss]]: Can be very helpful as they can deal with a massive stack of R.Osts in seconds.

